# Line endings.
#
# This repository is authored on Windows and deployed to Linux — the on-prem
# package is copied to the server by zip, USB or scp. A shell script checked
# out with CRLF arrives there broken, failing as
#
#   ./backup.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# which reads as a missing interpreter rather than a line-ending problem.
# Forcing LF on everything the server executes or parses removes that entirely.

* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is the exception: it runs on Windows, where CRLF is conventional.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
